6	//!
7	//! **Rust decides, Metal does** (spec §7): a look is defined here, as Color's
8	//! four keys, Light's nine and a [`SplitTone`], and published in the recipe
9	//! as that definition; the app bakes it on the GPU into a 33³ lattice with
10	//! the layer stage's own functions and mixes it at step 4d. Nothing here is
11	//! a colour table: the eight are Frame Job's own first numbers (tuned by the
12	//! owner at GR7), built from the textbook operations tone already uses — the
13	//! Concat rule (`designs/adr/effects-survey.md`) stands.
14	//!
15	//! Re-exported whole by `model_props.rs`, which `model.rs` re-exports whole
16	//! in turn, so `crate::model::Look` resolves like every other property type.
17	//!
18	//! **The declaration ORDER of [`LookKind`] is the gallery's and the menu's**
19	//! (GR-7): append, never reorder; `Lut` comes last and is not one of
20	//! [`LookKind::BUILT_IN`]. The JSON spelling of each variant is persisted, so
21	//! a rename needs a migration step. Closed: a misspelt kind is refused at the
22	//! serde boundary naming the nine, because there is no neutral look to fall
