211	//! `.cube` LUTs as media and as looks (spec §11 GR-8): the rules a `lut`
212	//! media row and a `video.look {kind: "lut", media}` obey, written once for
213	//! every door that meets them.
214	//!
215	//! - **The row.** A LUT is media so it is referenced, relinked and
216	//!   consolidated like footage, but it has no picture of its own: its row
217	//!   carries no video, audio, alpha or duration ([`check_lut_fields`], which
218	//!   `edit_track.rs`'s `check_media_fields` calls for `add_media`, a
219	//!   relink's probe and a pasted media row), and it is never placed as a clip — `add_clip`,
220	//!   `insert_clip`, `overwrite_clip` and `add_background` answer
221	//!   [`lut_not_placeable`].
222	//! - **The look.** `media` is required with `lut` and goes with nothing
223	//!   else, and must name a `lut` media of the project
224	//!   ([`Project::check_look_media`], beside `check_adjustment_video` on the
225	//!   patch path and on every pasted group, and in `validate` for a file),
226	//!   through [`Project::check_lut_reference`], which `media_color.rs`'s
227	//!   `color.lut` shares. A
228	//!   patch naming a built-in kind and no `media` drops a stored one
229	//!   ([`normalise_look`]), so a built-in kind on a LUT clip replaces the LUT.
230	//! - **An action's end** is never checked against the media list
231	//!   (`set_action_end` checks shape only), so an end may name a LUT that is
232	//!   not there: the evaluator reads such a look as NO look
233	//!   ([`Project::evaluates_as_look`]), and `actions.rs` switches `media` at
234	//!   the end like a `kind`, so an id is never interpolated.
235	//! - **Removing a used LUT** ([`Project::remove_lut`]) refuses naming the
236	//!   clips whose base look it is and the media whose Camera Log it is (spec
237	//!   §11 GR-16, `media.color.lut`), or with `with_clips` clears those looks
238	//!   and conversions and keeps the clips and the media; ends are left alone
239	//!   (inert by the evaluator).
240	//! - **Paste** brings a LUT's row by path like any media; an id the payload
241	//!   does not carry becomes no look ([`remap_look_media`]) rather than
242	//!   another media's id.
243	
244	use std::collections::HashMap;
245	
246	use serde_json::Value;
247	
248	use crate::export_overrides::spelled;
249	use crate::model::{Clip, Look, LookKind, Media, MediaKind, Project, VideoProps};
250	use crate::outcome::Outcome;
